<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine crops little affected by rain.</title>
<headline>Argentine crops little affected by rain.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's developing maize, sunflower and soybean crops were little affected by rains in the grain belt early Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;There's not much impact. The crops are coming along nicely,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>The Argentine Air Force's Meteorological Service forecast slightly cooler weather in the grain belt, with some showers but a tendency for the weather to clear later in the day in Buenos Aires, Santa Fe and Entre Rios.</p>
<p>Weather Services Corporation forecast highs of 75-85 F (24-29C) in grain areas.</p>
<p>((--Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
